// A declared datatype and its constructors (ADR-80; ADR-54 §3).
//
// The nested generator block `data Maybe(a : Type) : Type { None : Maybe(a);
// Some : (x : a) --> Maybe(a); }` mints a fresh generative-nominal type: the
// head binds the parameter once as a typed binder and declares the index
// arity (`: Type` when unindexed), and every generator's result head is the
// family applied to the parameter variable. Its two constructors build
// values, and `case` eliminates them by matching on the constructor. Unlike
// the built-in `Inl`/`Inr` sum, the nominal identity is the point -- a
// `Maybe` is not interchangeable with any structurally-identical declaration.
//
// A constructor application `Some(3)` only *checks* (like an injection): from
// `Some(3)` alone the type argument `a` is not inferable, so the value carries
// a `: Maybe(Integer)` ascription. The `case` body's result type comes from the
// function header's `-> F Integer`.
data Maybe(a : Type) : Type {
  None : Maybe(a);
  Some : (x : a) --> Maybe(a);
}

def unwrap_or_zero() -> F Integer {
  case (Some(3) : Maybe(Integer)) {
    None => ret 0,
    Some(x) => ret x
  }
}

unwrap_or_zero()

// The harness checks:
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-def: unwrap_or_zero
//@ expect-last-value: 3
